            <ArticleTitle>[Necrotic angiodermatitis: evaluation of an early skin graft treatment].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>567-70</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.anplas.2009.03.002</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Necrotic angio-dermatitis is a quite frequent ischemic ulceration found in various skin microvessels diseases. It usually occurs in elderly over 60 years particularly on legs. Lesions are rapidly spreading and very painful, without any response to common pain medicines. We went, through our 21 cases series, to confirm the analgesic effect of early excision and skin grafting.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
